window.SEARCH_INDEX = [{"url":"index.html","page":"Introduction","section":"","text":"Decisium From behavioral specification to intelligent execution. Semantic UI testing with decision models. Decisium runs Gherkin features written in plain English against a real browser. You write When I schedule the campaign , not selectors. Each Step is executed by Jev , TypeSafe's decision model. Jev does not generate text or code: it picks among the options Decisium enumerates from the page (the elements, the actions, the check kinds) and returns a probability for each. Decisium's code, not the model, decides whether a Step passed. No LLM, no prompts, no hallucinated selectors. See How a Step runs for the questions it is asked and how many requests a Step takes. @url:https://shop.example.com Feature: Checkout Scenario: Buy a backpack When I add the \"Backpack\" to the cart And I check out with email \"ada@example.com\" Then the order status should be \"Confirmed\" No selectors. Steps name what the user wants. Jev picks the element by meaning, among the ones on the page. Record and replay. What each Step resolved to is saved in a cassette next to the feature. CI replays it with zero model calls, and a real UI change fails as UI_CHANGED . Built on cucumber-js and Playwright. Your cucumber configuration, formatters, profiles and step definitions keep working. Agent-ready failures. A failed run writes report.md : the Step, the model's answers, the page text and a rerun command, ready for a coding agent. Next: Installation , then the Quick start ."},{"url":"installation.html","page":"Installation","section":"","text":"Installation Needs Node 22.18+ (or 23.6+). npm install --save-dev decisium npx playwright install chromium Live runs call Jev, TypeSafe's decision model, through the TypeSafe API: you need a TypeSafe API key. Decisium's code is MIT; Jev is TypeSafe's hosted service under its own terms. Set the key in the environment or in a .env file in the directory you run from: echo 'TYPESAFE_API_KEY=...' >> .env A replay ( --record none ) makes no model calls and does not need the key."},{"url":"installation.html#check-the-setup","page":"Installation","section":"Check the setup","text":"npx decisium doctor features/checkout.feature doctor checks Node, Chromium and the key (one tiny Jev call). Given features, it also opens every start URL. Each check prints [OK] or [FAIL] ; the exit code is 2 when one fails."},{"url":"installation.html#what-is-sent-to-jev","page":"Installation","section":"What is sent to Jev","text":"On a live run, per Turn: the Step's text and a text snapshot of the page (Playwright's accessibility tree: roles, names, visible text, link URLs), plus the message of an open browser dialog. No screenshots, no cookies, no network traffic. \"$NAME\" secrets are sent as the token only; the value never leaves your machine, and is masked back wherever the page shows it. A value written literally in a Step is sent to Jev, recorded in the cassette and written to log.txt . Replays ( --record none ) send nothing."},{"url":"quick-start.html","page":"Quick start","section":"","text":"Quick start"},{"url":"quick-start.html#1-write-a-feature","page":"Quick start","section":"1. Write a feature","text":"# features/campaign.feature @url:http://localhost:3000 Feature: Campaigns Scenario: Schedule a campaign When I enter \"Autumn Sale\" as the campaign name And I set the activation period to 2 weeks And I schedule the campaign Then the campaign status should be \"Scheduled\" The @url: tag is the start URL (a URL or a local HTML file). Each Scenario starts from a fresh browser. Quote every value a Step types or a check compares."},{"url":"quick-start.html#2-lint-it","page":"Quick start","section":"2. Lint it","text":"npx decisium lint features/campaign.feature No browser, no model: shows how each Step will be read and flags wordings Writing Steps marks as ones to avoid."},{"url":"quick-start.html#3-run-it-live","page":"Quick start","section":"3. Run it live","text":"npx decisium run features/campaign.feature The first run asks Jev for every Step and records the answers in features/campaign.cassette.json . Commit it."},{"url":"quick-start.html#4-replay-it","page":"Quick start","section":"4. Replay it","text":"npx decisium run features/campaign.feature --record none Every Step replays its recorded resolution with zero model calls. Use this in CI . When a Step fails, read Reports and debugging . When a wording does not work, look it up in the Writing Steps and Troubleshooting ."},{"url":"writing-features.html","page":"Features and scenarios","section":"","text":"Features and scenarios A Decisium test is an ordinary Gherkin .feature file. Every line no client step of yours matches is run by Decisium. @url:http://localhost:3000 Feature: Campaigns Background: When I start a new campaign Scenario: Schedule a campaign When I enter \"Winter Sale\" as the campaign name And I set the activation period to 2 weeks And I schedule the campaign Then the campaign status should be \"Scheduled\" Scenario Outline: Name validation When I try to save the draft with the name \"<name>\" Then the error should say \"<error>\" Examples: | name | error | | x | Name is too short | Start URL: @url: on the feature or a scenario (a URL or a local HTML file), or --url . More tags set the viewport, locale, time zone and geolocation: Browser context . Isolation: each scenario, and each Examples row of an outline, runs in a fresh browser. Background Steps run before each scenario. Steps: each line is an action (it changes the page) or a check (code verifies what the page shows). How to word them: Writing Steps . Tables and doc strings work as in cucumber: Data tables . One scenario: npx decisium run file.feature:12 runs only the scenario (or Examples row) at line 12."},{"url":"writing-features.html#how-a-step-runs","page":"Features and scenarios","section":"How a Step runs","text":"Decisium reads the page as text: its accessibility tree (roles, names, text, states). For an action, Jev picks one of the actions that page offers (click this button, type this quoted value into this field, press a named key, go back, …). Decisium performs it and reads the page again, until the task is done. For a check, Jev picks the subject and the kind of check; code compares the quoted value with the page. What each Step resolved to is saved in a cassette , so the next run can replay it without Jev. Jev never writes code or selectors; it only chooses among options Decisium lists, so a Step can only act on what is really on the page."},{"url":"steps.html","page":"Writing Steps","section":"","text":"Writing Steps A Step is one line of a scenario, written the way a user would describe the task. Decisium reads each line as an action (it changes the page) or a check (it verifies what the page shows). This page lists what each kind can do and how to word it. npx decisium lint <file.feature> flags the wordings marked Avoid below."},{"url":"steps.html#rules-of-thumb","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Rules of thumb","text":"One Step, one task , named by what the user wants, not by the clicks: I save the draft , not I click the button labelled Save draft . Quote every value : what to type, the option to pick, the text a check expects. Decisium only uses values you quoted; it never invents one. A number with a unit can stay unquoted ( 2 weeks ). A check quotes exactly what it compares : one value for a value check, the text to look for in a presence check. Name things the way the page labels them : \"heading\", \"error\", \"status\", \"the calendar\". Avoid words that also name something else; \"title\" can also mean the browser tab's title. Say \"open\" when you mean open. \"Search for\" runs a search; it does not open a result. Write \"$NAME\" for secrets. See Secrets . No CSS or XPath selectors. Quote what the page shows ( the \"Search page\" link ). When no wording works, write a client step ."},{"url":"steps.html#actions","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Actions","text":"An action Step runs in Turns: each Turn Jev picks one action among the elements on the page, Decisium performs it, and the Step ends once the task is done. Several clicks in one Step are fine when they serve one task: I delete the campaign opens the \"More actions\" menu first. A live action waits for the requests it started to finish (up to 5 s), so the next Step sees their result. A replay waits like a Playwright spec instead: see Waiting on replay . A Step may finish the task in the Step after it: I publish the post also confirms its dialog. Do not split what one task covers; quote the control instead: I publish the post, confirming with \"Publish now\" . A click never lands on a lookalike of a quoted control: when the Step quotes \"Publish now\" and Jev picks \"Publish again\" (a shared word, plus one the quote lacks), the Step fails as AMBIGUOUS and nothing is clicked. A control made only of the quote's words (\"Publish\") may lead to it, and a control in the quoted row or card (its \"Delete\") is that row's."},{"url":"steps.html#navigate","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Navigate","text":"Write Why I open the calendar Names the place, not the link. I open the \"Spring Sale\" campaign The quoted name picks the row. I start a new campaign The task, not the button text. I open the \"Ada Lovelace\" article through the search Says how and that it opens: types, submits, then opens the result. I go to \"/settings\" A path, query ( \"?tab=2\" ), #hash or full URL opens directly, relative to the start URL. I go back , I go forward , I reload the page Done directly, without the model. I open the contacts A link that opens a new tab: the following Steps act in the new tab. I close the tab , I switch back to the previous tab Done directly. Say them as their own Step. Avoid I search for \"Ada Lovelace\" when you want the article: the search runs, the result is never opened."},{"url":"steps.html#type","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Type","text":"Write Why I enter \"Winter Sale\" as the campaign name Value quoted, field named. I set the activation date to \"2026-12-01\" Dates in the format the field takes. I search for \"Ada\" and submit the search \"and submit\" makes typing alone not enough. I clear the Search field Types an empty value. After typing, Decisium leaves the field (so on-leave validation runs) and checks that the field holds the value; if it does not, the Step fails as ACTION_FAILED . Native inputs take ISO values: date \"2026-10-20\" , time \"14:30\" , datetime-local \"2026-10-20T14:30\" . Custom date pickers are clicked like any widget. A range input (slider) is filled like a text field: I set the volume to \"75\" ."},{"url":"steps.html#select","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Select","text":"I set the activation period to 2 weeks : a native select's options are the choices; the value can be quoted or a number with a unit. Decisium checks the option was chosen."},{"url":"steps.html#submit-and-act","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Submit and act","text":"I save the draft , I schedule the campaign , I delete the campaign . Name the task; Decisium finds the control."},{"url":"steps.html#attempt","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Attempt","text":"A Step starting with \"try\" or \"attempt\" is done once the action ran, even if the app refuses it. Use it for negative paths and check the refusal after it: When I try to schedule the campaign Then the error should say \"Set an activation date before scheduling\""},{"url":"steps.html#radios-and-toggles","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Radios and toggles","text":"Write Why I accept the terms Clicking a checkbox, switch or radio means \"on\"; Decisium reads the box after the click. I turn off dark mode Disable, turn off, decline, reject, opt out, unsubscribe mean \"off\". I choose Express shipping A radio is done once it is checked. I check \"Weekly digest\" , I uncheck \"Newsletter\" Decided by code, when the Step does nothing else. Already in the wanted state: the Step is done without a click. Avoid I check \"Weekly digest\" and save : split it."},{"url":"steps.html#keys","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Keys","text":"A key is pressed only when the Step names it after \"press\" or \"hit\": Playwright's names ( Escape , Tab , ArrowDown , PageDown , Home , F2 , …), aliases ( Esc , down arrow , Return , Space ) and + combinations ( Ctrl+K , Shift+Tab ; Ctrl is Control, Cmd is Meta). The key goes to whatever has focus. Write Why I press Escape Only a key: pressed directly, without the model. I open the command palette by pressing Ctrl+K The key is offered next to the page's elements. I press the down arrow , I press \"Tab\" Aliases and quotes both work. Avoid I close the help with the Escape key : without \"press\" or \"hit\" no key is pressed."},{"url":"steps.html#hover","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Hover","text":"I hover over the help button : say \"hover\" for a tooltip or a menu that opens on mouse-over; a plain click would close it again. What the hover shows is then part of the page: the tooltip should say \"Opens the docs\" . A title attribute needs no hover: the Save button's tooltip should be \"Save your work\" ."},{"url":"steps.html#double-click-right-click-drag-and-sliders","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Double-click, right-click, drag and sliders","text":"Write Why I double-click the note title and change it to \"Groceries\" Say the edit in the same Step, not just the double-click. I right-click report.pdf and choose \"Delete\" The custom context menu is used in the next Turn. I drag \"Fix bug\" to the Done list Decisium picks where to drop it among the page's areas. I set the volume to \"75\" A slider is filled with the quoted value."},{"url":"steps.html#scroll-inside-lists-and-panels","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Scroll inside lists and panels","text":"I scroll down the Inbox until \"Message 15\" is shown , I scroll up the Chat until \"Chat line 5\" is shown . A panel that scrolls on its own is offered as a target. Content already rendered is visible without scrolling; only lazy-loaded content needs it."},{"url":"steps.html#files-and-downloads","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Files and downloads","text":"Write Why I upload \"notes.txt\" with the Attach file button \"upload\" or \"attach\" plus a quoted path (relative to the feature file). Hidden file inputs work. I export the contacts as CSV The download is saved to the scenario's run folder. the downloaded file name should be \"contacts.csv\" The last download's name. the downloaded file should contain \"Ada Lovelace,engineer\" A text file's contents; binary files only by name."},{"url":"steps.html#clipboard","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Clipboard","text":"Write Why I copy the invite link Clicked like any button; the page may use the clipboard. the copied text should be \"https://example.com/invite/7f3a\" What was copied during the scenario. I paste into the message box Pastes the clipboard (Ctrl/Cmd+V). With a quoted value it types it instead."},{"url":"steps.html#browser-dialogs","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Browser dialogs","text":"alert , confirm , prompt and \"Leave site?\" are answered by the Step that opens them: OK (or leave) only when the Step clearly means it, otherwise Cancel. An alert is closed. A prompt gets the Step's quoted value. Until the next action, the dialog's message can be checked. Write Why I delete the \"Groceries\" note Clicks Delete, then confirms: the Step asks for the deletion. I start deleting the \"Ideas\" note but cancel Says to cancel: Cancel. I rename the list to \"Errands\" The prompt gets the quoted value. the confirm should say \"Delete the Groceries note?\" The last dialog's message. I leave by the \"Search page\" link \"Leave site?\" is accepted because the Step means to leave. Avoid I accept the confirm as its own Step: the Step before already answered it. Say the intent in the Step that opens the dialog."},{"url":"steps.html#iframes-and-web-components","page":"Writing Steps","section":"iframes and web components","text":"Elements inside iframes and open shadow roots are part of the page like any other: no frame or component to name. I enter \"ada@example.com\" in Email works when the field is in an iframe."},{"url":"steps.html#checks","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Checks","text":"A check is decided by code, not by the model. Jev only identifies what to look at (the subject) and what kind of check it is; code then compares. A check that cannot be compared is UNVERIFIABLE , not passed. Like Playwright's expect , a check that does not pass yet is retried each time the page changes, until it passes or the page has nothing left pending (up to 5 s). A check that already holds passes at once, so check what only the new state shows."},{"url":"steps.html#value-checks","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Value checks","text":"Write Why the campaign status should be \"Draft\" One subject, one quoted value. the error should say \"Set an activation date before scheduling\" the activation period should be \"2 weeks\" Reads a select's chosen option. the Email field should be \"ada@example.com\" A field's current value. The subject is picked by meaning: if the status says \"Draft\" while a filter elsewhere says \"Scheduled\", the campaign status should be \"Scheduled\" correctly fails. Avoid : the article title should be \"Ada Lovelace\" (\"title\" is also the tab's title; say \"heading\"), … should be \"Ada\" or \"Ada Lovelace\" (exactly one value), the article should be well written (subjective; see Judged checks )."},{"url":"steps.html#presence","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Presence","text":"Write Why \"Saved\" should appear The text anywhere on the page. the article should say \"born 10 December 1815\" The text anywhere in the subject. \"Charles Babbage\" should not appear in the results Absence. Avoid the results should be shown : it quotes nothing to look for."},{"url":"steps.html#scoped-presence","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Scoped presence","text":"\"Winter Sale\" should appear in the calendar , \"Spring Sale\" should not appear in the campaign list . Only text inside the named area counts; the same name in a toast elsewhere does not. The area must be on the screen: open it first."},{"url":"steps.html#state-checks","page":"Writing Steps","section":"State checks","text":"the \"Schedule\" button should be disabled , \"Newsletter\" should be unchecked . States: disabled, enabled, checked, unchecked, expanded, collapsed, selected, pressed. An unquoted name works when it is unique."},{"url":"steps.html#memory","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Memory","text":"A check may refer back to a value an earlier Step quoted: after I enter \"Winter Sale\" as the campaign name , the campaign should appear in the calendar looks for \"Winter Sale\". When the scenario quoted several values and it is unclear which one is meant, the check is UNVERIFIABLE : quote the value."},{"url":"steps.html#judged-checks","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Judged checks","text":"A subjective check ( the article should be well written ) cannot be compared by code. With --judged , Jev judges it and the result is reported as JUDGED_PASSED or JUDGED_FAILED , never as a plain pass."},{"url":"steps.html#marginal-passes","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Marginal passes","text":"A check that passed while the model was barely sure what it was looking at is reported as a marginal pass : passed, with a warning. Treat it like an unclear wording and make the Step more specific; --strict fails it as AMBIGUOUS ."},{"url":"steps.html#more","page":"Writing Steps","section":"More","text":""},{"url":"steps.html#data-tables","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Data tables","text":"An action's table runs one Step per row: When I fill in the new contact: | First name | Ada | | Last name | Lovelace | Two columns are label/value pairs, one column is a list of values, three or more columns are rows under a header row. A check's table is matched row by row to a table on the page by column header (extra rows and any order pass; say \"exactly\" or \"in this order\" to be strict). A one-column check table lists values that must all be shown; \"should not show:\" checks that none is. Absence of table rows cannot be checked. Table cells cannot be empty or contain \" . A doc string is one more quoted value, line breaks kept: When I write the notes: \"\"\" Wrote the first program. Born in London. \"\"\""},{"url":"steps.html#secrets","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Secrets","text":"Write \"$NAME\" in a Step's quotes: I log in as \"$SAUCE_USER\" with password \"$SAUCE_PASSWORD\" . The value comes from the environment or .env and is typed into the page; the model, logs, traces and cassettes only see the token, and it is masked back wherever the page shows it. A missing variable is a setup error. A scenario that typed a secret keeps no Playwright trace. Password fields are always masked. A value written literally in a Step is sent to the model and recorded."},{"url":"steps.html#out-of-scope","page":"Writing Steps","section":"Out of scope","text":"Canvas drawing, maps, captchas, 2FA codes and closed shadow roots cannot be seen or driven by Steps. Use a test mode in the app, or a client step (for example, compute a 2FA code from its secret)."},{"url":"how-it-works.html","page":"How a Step runs","section":"","text":"How a Step runs Decisium reads the page, lists what is on it, and asks Jev questions whose answers are picks among that list. Jev never writes code or values; every answer comes back as a probability per option. Decisium's code then checks the confidence, performs the action with Playwright and decides pass or fail. A question is asked in a request : one call to Jev carrying the Step's text, a text snapshot of the page ( ui ) and one or more questions. Questions in the same request read the same page, so their answers are consistent."},{"url":"how-it-works.html#an-action-step","page":"How a Step runs","section":"An action Step","text":"An action Step runs in Turns . Each Turn is one request with three questions: Question Options Answer used for Given the actions taken for the Step so far, does ui show the Step is fully accomplished? yes/no, as a probability ending the Step Which element in ui should be interacted with next? every actionable element, plus \"the page itself\" and \"none\" the target How should that element be used? click, type, select, hover, press a key, scroll… the action Then code decides, in this order: Done? done ≥ 0.8 ends the Step. After an action that changed the page, done ≥ 0.5 with target \"none\" is enough. Sure of the target? The top element needs ≥ 0.5 ( confidence.target ) and a lead of ≥ 0.1 over the next; otherwise AMBIGUOUS . Target \"none\" is BLOCKED . The right control? A click on a lookalike of a quoted control (\"Publish again\" when the Step quotes \"Publish now\") is AMBIGUOUS , and nothing is clicked. Act. Playwright performs it, waits for the requests it started, and the next Turn reads the new page. A Step gets at most 8 Turns ( maxTurns ; then STEP_TIMEOUT ). After each action Decisium waits up to 5 s ( actionTimeout ) for requests and DOM changes to settle. Some actions add one request: When Extra question The action types, selects or uploads Which value should be entered into the element? Options: the Step's quoted values, numbers and Doc string, plus \"none\". A browser dialog is open How should it be answered? Options: OK / Cancel, or one of the quoted values for a prompt. The action is a drag Onto which element should it be dropped? I press Escape , I go back , I go to \"/settings\" ask nothing: code does them directly."},{"url":"how-it-works.html#example","page":"How a Step runs","section":"Example","text":"From a live run of When I delete the campaign in the demo app ( npm run example:server , test/fixtures/campaign-manager ): Turn Page done target Code 1 Campaign page 0.04 button \"More actions\" 0.99 click \"More actions\" 2 Menu open: \"Delete campaign\" 0.03 menuitem \"Delete campaign\" 1.00 click \"Delete campaign\" 3 Campaign list, toast \"deleted\" 0.98 none 0.86 DONE 3 requests. done stayed low with the menu open because nothing was deleted yet: a Step continues until its task is done, so a following I click \"Delete campaign\" would have nothing left to do."},{"url":"how-it-works.html#a-check","page":"How a Step runs","section":"A check","text":"A check is one request with four questions; Jev only says what to look at, code compares: Question Options What kind of check is it? value, presence, absence, state, fuzzy Which element is the check about? every element with text, plus \"none\" Which control state does it require? checked, disabled, expanded, selected… Where does it say to look? the page's lists, tables, sections, dialogs; \"anywhere\" or \"named area missing\" Code then reads the element and compares it with the quoted value. A check that does not pass yet is asked again each time the page changes, up to 5 s ( checkTimeout ): one more request per change. A check that quotes nothing first asks which value from an earlier Step it refers to (one more request). A judged check adds a fifth question: does ui satisfy the check?"},{"url":"how-it-works.html#large-pages","page":"How a Step runs","section":"Large pages","text":"More than 255 candidates (a choice question's limit): they are asked in batches, the top 3 of each batch are kept, and the real question is asked over what is left. A page with 336 links costs 2 more requests. A snapshot over about 80,000 characters : it is cut into sections and Jev picks the sections the Step needs, before the questions above. More requests, once per Step and page."},{"url":"how-it-works.html#how-many-requests","page":"How a Step runs","section":"How many requests","text":"Typical counts: Step Requests Action done in one click 2 (act, then confirm done) Action through a menu or dialog 3 or more Type into a field + 1 per value typed Check that passes at once 1 The demo app's first scenario (create, schedule and find a campaign; 11 Steps), run live: 21 requests , about 24,000 input and 4,400 output tokens. Each typed or selected value took 3 (act, value, done). Replays ( --record none ) send no request: the cassette holds each Step's answers. See Record and replay ."},{"url":"how-it-works.html#where-to-see-it","page":"How a Step runs","section":"Where to see it","text":"log.txt in the run directory: every Turn's page, Decision: done=… action: … target: … and what was executed. trace.jsonl : per Step jevCalls , inputTokens and outputTokens . report.md : for a failed Step, Jev's answers with the top three options each."},{"url":"browser-context.html","page":"Browser context","section":"","text":"Browser context Each scenario starts in a fresh browser. Tags on the feature or the scenario set up that browser before the first page opens. When the same tag is on both, the scenario's wins; when a tag repeats, the last one wins. Tag Effect @url:<url|file> The start URL: a URL or a local HTML file (relative to where you run). --url overrides it. @viewport:390x844 Window size in pixels. @viewport:iPhone-13 A Playwright device (dashes for spaces): size, user agent and touch. @locale:de-DE Browser language and number/date formats. @timezone:Europe/Berlin Time zone. @geolocation:52.52,13.40 Position (latitude, longitude); the location permission is granted. @replay-network:<glob> Records and replays matching browser requests. See Network replay . @url:https://shop.example.com @locale:de-DE Feature: Shop in German @viewport:iPhone-13 Scenario: Checkout on a phone When I add the \"Backpack\" to the cart Then the cart badge should show \"1\" Anything else about the browser (cookies, storage, permissions, mocked requests, a logged-in session) is set up with a client step ."},{"url":"client-steps.html","page":"Client steps","section":"","text":"Client steps Your own cucumber step definitions run next to Decisium. A line one of them matches runs your code ; every other line goes to Jev. Use them for setup the page cannot do (cookies, API login, mocks), for anything out of scope for Steps, and as the fallback when no wording works. // steps/campaigns.steps.ts import { Given } from \"@cucumber/cucumber\"; import type { BrowserContext } from \"playwright\"; Given(\"the campaigns API returns {string}\", async function (this: { context: BrowserContext }, name: string) { await this.context.route(\"**/api/campaigns\", route => route.fulfill({ json: [{ id: 1, name, status: \"Draft\" }] })); }); Scenario: The list shows what the API returns Given the campaigns API returns \"Mocked Sale\" When I click Load campaigns Then \"Mocked Sale\" should be shown Load them with --import (repeatable) or import in your configuration : npx decisium run features/campaigns.feature --import steps/campaigns.steps.ts A client step makes no model call and is not recorded in the cassette."},{"url":"client-steps.html#the-world","page":"Client steps","section":"The World","text":"Property What it is this.page The current tab, a Playwright Page . A popup the app opens becomes the current tab. this.context The scenario's Playwright BrowserContext . Client steps run after the start page has opened, so a mock covers requests made from then on (for example, by the next click)."},{"url":"client-steps.html#recipes","page":"Client steps","section":"Recipes","text":"Need Code Mock a request this.context.route(glob, route => route.fulfill({ json })) Cookies this.context.addCookies([{ name, value, url }]) , then this.page.reload() if the page already read them Local storage this.page.evaluate(([k, v]) => localStorage.setItem(k, v), [key, value]) , then this.page.reload() Log in through the API await this.context.request.post(url, { data }) shares cookies with the page; then reload. Faster than the form. Permissions this.context.grantPermissions([\"clipboard-read\"]) A second user const other = await this.context.browser()!.newContext() , then await other.newPage() . Steps act on this.page only; drive and check the other user's page in code. Wait for a request Nothing to write: a live action waits for the requests it started (up to 5 s); on replay the next action waits for its element and a check retries until it passes. Hooks ( Before , After , …) and anything else cucumber offers work too."},{"url":"cli.html","page":"Command line","section":"","text":"Command line decisium step \"<step>\" --url <url|file> [--headed] [--judged] [--strict] [-v] [--debug] decisium run <file.feature[:line]>... [--url <url|file>] [--headed] [--judged] [--strict] [--record <mode>] [--parallel <n|auto>] [--report-dir <dir>] [--confidence-target <p>] [--confidence-answer <p>] [--check-timeout <ms>] [--action-timeout <ms>] [--max-turns <n>] [--format <name[:path]>] [--import <file>] [-p <profile>] [--no-agent-report] [-v] [--debug] decisium doctor [<file.feature>...] decisium lint <file.feature>..."},{"url":"cli.html#run","page":"Command line","section":"run","text":"Runs features. file.feature:line runs only the scenario (or Examples row) at that line. Flag --url <url|file> Start URL; overrides @url: tags. --record new|none|all Cassette mode, see Record and replay . Default new . --parallel <n|auto> Worker processes. Features run side by side, a feature's scenarios in order. Only for features that do not share app state. auto : min(CPUs, 4) with Jev, every CPU with --record none . --report-dir <dir> Where run folders are written. Default runs . --confidence-target <p> How sure Jev must be of the element an action acts on, in (0, 1]. Default 0.5. --confidence-answer <p> How sure Jev must be of every other answer, in (0, 1]. Default 0.8; lower warns. --check-timeout <ms> How long a check waits for the expected state. Default 5000. --action-timeout <ms> How long after an action to wait for the page to settle. Default 5000. --max-turns <n> Actions a Step may take before STEP_TIMEOUT , 1-20. Default 8. --headed Show the browser. --judged Let Jev judge fuzzy checks. They report JUDGED_PASSED / JUDGED_FAILED , never PASSED . --strict A check that passed on a barely-confident answer (a \"marginal pass\") fails as AMBIGUOUS . --format <name[:path]> Any cucumber formatter, e.g. junit:junit.xml . Repeatable. --import <file> Your own step definitions or hooks. Repeatable. -p <profile> A cucumber profile. Repeatable. --no-agent-report Do not write report.md . -v Print every Observation and Jev answer (always saved to log.txt ). --debug Show stack traces."},{"url":"cli.html#step","page":"Command line","section":"step","text":"Runs one Step against a URL, without a feature file. Handy for trying a wording. npx decisium step \"I open the calendar\" --url http://localhost:3000"},{"url":"cli.html#doctor","page":"Command line","section":"doctor","text":"Checks Node, Chromium and TYPESAFE_API_KEY ; given features, also opens every start URL."},{"url":"cli.html#lint","page":"Command line","section":"lint","text":"No browser, no model. Per Step: its kind, the quoted values, keys, secret placeholders, and warnings for wordings the Writing Steps marks as ones to avoid."},{"url":"cli.html#exit-codes","page":"Command line","section":"Exit codes","text":"0 passed, 1 a scenario failed, 2 configuration or infrastructure error."},{"url":"record-replay.html","page":"Record and replay","section":"","text":"Record and replay What each Step resolved to (the element's role, name, container and position, and the values) is recorded in <file>.cassette.json next to the feature. On the next run it is replayed without Jev while exactly one element on the page still matches it. --record Behaviour new (default) Replay; resolve new or no-longer-matching Steps live and write them back (reported as healed ). none Replay only. A missing or broken resolution fails as UI_CHANGED . Use in CI. all Resolve everything live and rewrite the cassette. The run summary says what happened: Cassette features/campaign.cassette.json: 2 replayed, 0 recorded, 0 healed"},{"url":"record-replay.html#workflow","page":"Record and replay","section":"Workflow","text":"Record once with --record new (or all ), check the outcomes, commit the cassettes. Run CI with --record none : same outcome every run, zero model calls. When the UI really changes, CI fails as UI_CHANGED . Heal locally with --record new and commit the cassette. A live run asks Jev every time, so a Step close to the confidence gate can end differently from run to run. Replays do not. See Troubleshooting . Backend requests can be replayed too: Network replay ."},{"url":"record-replay.html#waiting-on-replay","page":"Record and replay","section":"Waiting on replay","text":"A replay waits the way a Playwright spec does, not after every action: An action does not wait for the page to settle. The next action waits until its recorded element is on the page. A check retries until it passes or the page has nothing left pending (up to 5 s). An action that shows no change yet waits for one before it counts as having done nothing. A request pending for over 1.5 s (a hung analytics or error-report call) stops counting as pending. A live run ( --record new or all ) also waits after each action for the requests it started (up to 5 s), so Jev sees the result."},{"url":"network-replay.html","page":"Network replay","section":"","text":"Network replay @replay-network:<glob> records the browser's requests that match the glob and replays them on later runs. Use it to make tests independent of a slow, costly or unstable backend, for example an app that calls an LLM. @replay-network:**/api/** Scenario: The assistant answers When I ask the assistant \"What is my balance?\" Then the answer should mention \"balance\" It follows --record , like the cassette : --record Network new (default) Replay the recording; record it if there is none. none Replay only. all Record again. The recording is <feature>.network/<scenario>.har next to the feature (response bodies in files beside it). Commit it with the cassette. Matching: a request is matched by method, URL and how many times that URL was called before, not by its body, so requests with timestamps or ids in them still replay. A matching request that is not in the recording fails the Step with \"network not in recording\" and is never sent to the real backend. Re-record with --record all . Limits: A streamed response (server-sent events) replays in one piece, so streamed text appears at once. WebSockets are not recorded. Only the browser's requests are recorded; requests your backend makes to other services are not."},{"url":"configuration.html","page":"Configuration","section":"","text":"Configuration and reporters decisium run loads configuration exactly like cucumber-js: your cucumber.{js,mjs,cjs,json,yaml} , -p <profile> , and cucumber's --format name[:path] and --import <file> flags, added to the file's values. Decisium adds its own step definitions to import ."},{"url":"configuration.html#decisium-options","page":"Configuration","section":"Decisium options","text":"In worldParameters.decisium , so raw npx cucumber-js reads them too. Flags ( --url , --record , --strict , ...) and DECISIUM_* env ( DECISIUM_URL , DECISIUM_RECORD , DECISIUM_STRICT=1 , ...) override them. // cucumber.mjs export default { worldParameters: { decisium: { record: \"none\", strict: true } }, // url, record, headed, judged, strict, verbose, debug, agentReport, // reportDir, confidence: { target, answer }, checkTimeout, actionTimeout, maxTurns }; Precedence: flag > DECISIUM_* env > worldParameters.decisium > default. A value of the wrong type or out of range fails at startup (exit 2). --parallel workers read the same values."},{"url":"configuration.html#tuning","page":"Configuration","section":"Tuning","text":"// cucumber.mjs export default { worldParameters: { decisium: { url: \"http://localhost:3000\", reportDir: \"e2e/runs\", confidence: { target: 0.6, answer: 0.85 }, checkTimeout: 10000, actionTimeout: 10000, maxTurns: 12, }, }, }; Option Default Flag Env Affects reportDir \"runs\" --report-dir DECISIUM_REPORT_DIR Where <reportDir>/<timestamp>/ (log, trace, screenshots, report.md ) is written. confidence.target 0.5 --confidence-target DECISIUM_CONFIDENCE_TARGET How sure Jev must be of the element an action acts on (and a drag's drop target). In (0, 1]. confidence.answer 0.8 --confidence-answer DECISIUM_CONFIDENCE_ANSWER Every other answer: a check's required state, the value to type or select, which earlier value a check refers to, a dialog answer. A pass under answer + 0.1 is marginal. In (0, 1]. checkTimeout 5000 --check-timeout DECISIUM_CHECK_TIMEOUT Ms a check waits for the page to reach the expected state. actionTimeout 5000 --action-timeout DECISIUM_ACTION_TIMEOUT Ms after an action to wait for requests and DOM changes to settle. maxTurns 8 --max-turns DECISIUM_MAX_TURNS Turns an action Step may take before STEP_TIMEOUT , 1-20. Only the top probability is configurable; the lead over the runner-up stays fixed (0.1 target, 0.3 answer): it is what catches \"two controls look the same\". Confidence affects live answers only (a replay reuses recorded resolutions); timeouts and maxTurns apply to replays too. The effective values go into the run event in trace.jsonl , and report.md says when confidence was not the default. When to change them: Slow app: raise checkTimeout and actionTimeout . Long flow in one Step (a wizard): raise maxTurns , or split the Step. AMBIGUOUS on a clear page: reword the Step first, then raise or lower confidence.target . Marginal passes: reword. Lowering confidence.answer below 0.8 prints a warning: a wrong reading can then pass."},{"url":"configuration.html#reporters","page":"Configuration","section":"Reporters","text":"Any cucumber formatter: cucumber's own junit , json , html , message , or a package such as the official Qase reporter. Only one formatter may write to stdout: one configured without a path takes it; otherwise Decisium's console output does. decisium run features/login.feature --format junit:reports/junit.xml"},{"url":"configuration.html#qase","page":"Configuration","section":"Qase","text":"Decisium ships nothing Qase-specific; wire the official reporter as in any cucumber project. npm install --save-dev cucumberjs-qase-reporter echo '{\"mode\":\"report\"}' > qase.config.json # or mode \"testops\" with QASE_TESTOPS_API_TOKEN, QASE_TESTOPS_PROJECT decisium run features/login.feature --format cucumberjs-qase-reporter:/dev/null Or in your configuration, which raw npx cucumber-js uses too: // cucumber.mjs export default { // Raw cucumber-js only: Decisium's steps and formatter (decisium run adds both itself). import: [\"node_modules/decisium/dist/steps.js\"], format: [\"decisium/formatter\", \"cucumberjs-qase-reporter:/dev/null\"], }; Tag scenarios @QaseID=<id> . A failing Step's message starts with its outcome; app failures ( ASSERTION_FAILED , JUDGED_FAILED , BLOCKED , ACTION_FAILED ) report as failed , every other outcome as invalid . A marginal pass reaches every reporter as a text/plain attachment marginal-pass.txt on its Step (Qase stores it as file.txt )."},{"url":"reports.html","page":"Reports and debugging","section":"","text":"Reports and debugging"},{"url":"reports.html#console","page":"Reports and debugging","section":"Console","text":"One line per Step, the reason under a failed one, and a Failures block at the end with a rerun command per failed scenario. A marginal pass (the check passed, but Jev was barely confident) is listed separately; treat it like an unclear wording, or fail it with --strict ."},{"url":"reports.html#the-run-directory","page":"Reports and debugging","section":"The run directory","text":"Each run writes <reportDir>/<timestamp>/ ( reportDir defaults to runs , see configuration ): trace.jsonl : Observations, Jev answers, actions and outcomes. Each scenario's result event has perf : milliseconds spent in observe , perform:<verb> , after:<verb> (waiting after an action) and settle , split by what held it ( settle:requests:<type> , settle:timers , settle:quiet ). log.txt : the full decision log (what -v prints). Per failed scenario: a screenshot per Turn (with --record none , of the failed Step only), playwright-trace.zip , console-errors.txt and ui.txt (the page text). Passed scenarios keep none. report.md when something failed: every failure with Jev's answers, the page text around it and a rerun command, for a coding agent. --no-agent-report turns it off."},{"url":"reports.html#outcomes","page":"Reports and debugging","section":"Outcomes","text":"Outcome Meaning PASSED / DONE The check held / the action finished. ASSERTION_FAILED The app is wrong: the value or text is not what the Step expects. BLOCKED , ACTION_FAILED The action could not be done. ELEMENT_NOT_FOUND Nothing on the page matches what the Step names. STEP_TIMEOUT The Step took too many Turns without finishing. PAGE_TOO_LARGE The page is over the model's request limit. AMBIGUOUS Jev could not tell which element the Step means. Reword. UNVERIFIABLE The check quotes nothing code can compare. Reword. UI_CHANGED A replayed resolution no longer matches the page ( --record none ). JUDGED_PASSED / JUDGED_FAILED A fuzzy check judged by Jev ( --judged ). The agent skill shows how to classify a failure: the app is wrong, or the wording is unclear."},{"url":"ci.html","page":"CI","section":"","text":"CI Replay committed cassettes: no model calls, no API key, the same outcome every run. # .github/workflows/e2e.yml name: e2e on: [push, pull_request] jobs: e2e: runs-on: ubuntu-latest steps: - uses: actions/checkout@v4 - uses: actions/setup-node@v4 with: { node-version: 24 } - run: npm ci - run: npx playwright install --with-deps chromium - run: npx decisium run features/*.feature --record none --parallel auto --format junit:reports/junit.xml - if: failure() uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4 with: { name: decisium-runs, path: runs/ } Upload runs/ (or your reportDir ) on failure: it holds the screenshots, Playwright trace and report.md for every failed scenario."},{"url":"cucumber-js.html","page":"Running with cucumber-js","section":"","text":"Running with cucumber-js decisium run already runs inside cucumber-js and loads your cucumber.{js,mjs,cjs,json,yaml} . Use raw npx cucumber-js only when your project already runs cucumber that way (CI scripts, IDE run buttons) and you want Decisium Steps in the same run as your own step definitions. // cucumber.mjs export default { import: [\"node_modules/decisium/dist/steps.js\", \"steps/**/*.js\"], format: [\"decisium/formatter\"], worldParameters: { decisium: { record: \"none\" } }, }; npx cucumber-js features/checkout.feature import takes file paths, not package names, hence the node_modules/... path. The options in worldParameters.decisium are the same as decisium run 's flags; see Configuration ."},{"url":"troubleshooting.html","page":"Troubleshooting","section":"","text":"Troubleshooting"},{"url":"troubleshooting.html#a-step-fails-sometimes-passes-other-times","page":"Troubleshooting","section":"A Step fails sometimes, passes other times","text":"A live run asks Jev every time, so a Step whose wording is borderline can end differently from run to run. Replay in CI. Record once, check the outcomes, commit the cassettes and run CI with --record none : every Step replays what it resolved to, with the same outcome every run. Live variation only matters while recording. See Record and replay . Read the reason, then reword. An AMBIGUOUS reason names what the Step could mean. Quote the one you mean: I leave for the search page can mean two links; I leave by the \"Search page\" link cannot. When it is unclear how (a Search button or Enter), say how: … and press Enter . Keep together what the page cannot do separately. If a filter only applies when Search is clicked, I filter the users by role \"Admin\" clicks it; a following I search has nothing left to do. AMBIGUOUS: Jev chose … which is not \"…\" after a Step that already did the task: the Step before it finished the job ( I publish the post confirmed the dialog), so I confirm with \"Publish now\" only finds a lookalike. Merge them: I publish the post, confirming with \"Publish now\" . Still unstable: a client step . Code can use any Playwright locator. Each one marks a gap worth reporting."},{"url":"troubleshooting.html#what-an-outcome-means-and-what-to-do","page":"Troubleshooting","section":"What an outcome means and what to do","text":"Outcome Usually Do ASSERTION_FAILED The app is wrong. Check the app, not the Step. AMBIGUOUS The Step could mean more than one thing. Name the element or area; quote its label. UNVERIFIABLE The check quotes nothing to compare. Quote the expected value or text. BLOCKED The task cannot be done on this page. Check the start URL and the Steps before it; a hover menu needs \"hover\". ELEMENT_NOT_FOUND Nothing matches what the Step names. Use the page's own label. ACTION_FAILED The action ran but did not take effect (e.g. a field rejected the value). Check the value's format; for dates use ISO. STEP_TIMEOUT The Step did not finish in its allowed actions. Split it into smaller tasks, or raise maxTurns for a long flow. UI_CHANGED A replayed Step no longer matches the page. If the change is intended, re-record with --record new . PAGE_TOO_LARGE The page is over the model's size limit. Test a narrower page or state. marginal pass Passed, but the model was barely sure. Make the Step more specific; do not lower confidence.answer . check fails on a slow page The expected state came after the check gave up. Raise checkTimeout (and actionTimeout if actions finish too early). Run npx decisium lint on the feature: it flags many of these wordings before you run."},{"url":"troubleshooting.html#why-not-selectors","page":"Troubleshooting","section":"Why not selectors","text":"Selectors tie a test to markup, skip the model, and do not help with the most common failure: deciding when a Step is done. Quote what the page shows instead."},{"url":"agent-skill.html","page":"Agent skill","section":"","text":"Agent skill Install it into your coding agent from node_modules/decisium/skills/decisium/SKILL.md . Decisium runs each Step by asking Jev, a decision model that only picks among offered answers; code decides pass/fail. A Step's wording decides most outcomes. The wording rules, per kind of Step, are in https://andletenkov.github.io/decisium/steps.html . Read it before writing a Step. This skill is the procedure."},{"url":"agent-skill.html#write","page":"Agent skill","section":"Write","text":"Write the feature: an @url:<start url> tag, then one Scenario per user journey, each starting from a fresh browser. Word each Step like a Write row of its kind (navigate, type, select, act, attempt, keys, value / presence / scoped / state check, memory, secrets). Quote every value the Step uses and every value a check compares. Credentials go in as \"$NAME\" placeholders, with the variables set in the environment or .env . Run npx decisium lint <file.feature> . It shows how each Step will be read (kind, quoted values, placeholders) and flags wordings to avoid with ⚠. Done when every ⚠ is reworded away, or kept on purpose with a # comment saying why."},{"url":"agent-skill.html#run-and-repair","page":"Agent skill","section":"Run and repair","text":"Run npx decisium run <file.feature> (live Jev the first time; it records a cassette next to the feature). On a failure, read runs/<id>/report.md : the Step at file:line , Jev's answers, the page text around the element, and a rerun command for that scenario. Classify each failure: The app is wrong (ASSERTION_FAILED, BLOCKED with the expected control truly missing): keep the Step, and report the app behaviour. The wording is unclear (AMBIGUOUS, UNVERIFIABLE, a check that picked the wrong element): reword using https://andletenkov.github.io/decisium/troubleshooting.html , then rerun just that scenario. AMBIGUOUS: Jev chose … which is not \"X\" usually means the Step before already used X (it finished the task): merge the two Steps, not an app bug. A marginal pass warning means the pass rested on a barely-confident answer. Treat it like an unclear wording. Keep the test's intent fixed while rewording. The quoted expected values and the area a check looks in stay as written. A rewording that makes a check pass by reading a different element (a link instead of the heading, a search box instead of the article) is a false pass. Compare Jev's subject in report.md with what the scenario means. Done when the run passes, or every remaining failure is classified as the app being wrong, with the evidence line from report.md ."},{"url":"examples.html","page":"Examples","section":"","text":"Examples Features against real public sites. Copy one into your project and run it: npx decisium run saucedemo.feature The first run calls Jev and writes saucedemo.cassette.json next to it; after that, --record none replays it with no model calls. How to word each kind of Step is in Writing Steps ."},{"url":"examples.html#saucedemo","page":"Examples","section":"saucedemo.feature","text":"A shop: login, a locked-out user, sorting, the cart and checkout validation. Source 1 @url:https://www.saucedemo.com/ 2 Feature: Sauce Demo shop (login, sorting, cart, checkout validation) 3 Demo credentials are listed on the login page. 4 5 Scenario: A locked out user cannot log in 6 When I try to log in as \"locked_out_user\" with password \"secret_sauce\" 7 Then the error should say \"Sorry, this user has been locked out.\" 8 9 Scenario: Sorting by price puts the cheapest product first 10 When I log in as \"standard_user\" with password \"secret_sauce\" 11 And I sort the products by \"Price (low to high)\" 12 Then the first product price should be \"$7.99\" 13 14 Scenario: The cart counts added products 15 When I log in as \"standard_user\" with password \"secret_sauce\" 16 And I add \"Sauce Labs Backpack\" to the cart 17 And I put \"Sauce Labs Bike Light\" in the cart 18 Then the cart badge should show \"2\" 19 20 Scenario: Checkout requires a first name, then completes 21 When I log in as \"standard_user\" with password \"secret_sauce\" 22 And I add \"Sauce Labs Backpack\" to the cart 23 And I open the cart 24 And I start the checkout 25 And I try to continue without filling in the form 26 Then the error should say \"First Name is required\" 27 When I enter \"Ada\" as first name, \"Lovelace\" as last name and \"10115\" as postal code 28 And I continue 29 Then the item total should be \"$29.99\" 30 When I finish the order 31 Then I should see \"Thank you for your order!\" 32"},{"url":"examples.html#todomvc","page":"Examples","section":"todomvc.feature","text":"List state: a Background, counters, filters and absence checks scoped to the list. Source 1 @url:https://demo.playwright.dev/todomvc/ 2 Feature: TodoMVC (list state, counters, filters) 3 4 Background: 5 When I add a todo \"Buy milk\" 6 And I add a todo \"Write report\" 7 And I add a todo \"Call mom\" 8 9 Scenario: Completing a todo updates the counter 10 When I mark \"Write report\" as completed 11 Then the counter should say \"2 items left\" 12 And \"Write report\" should be checked 13 14 Scenario: Filters show only matching todos 15 When I mark \"Buy milk\" as completed 16 And I show only the active todos 17 Then \"Buy milk\" should not appear in the todo list 18 And \"Call mom\" should appear in the todo list 19 20 Scenario: Clearing completed todos removes them 21 When I mark all todos as complete 22 And I clear the completed todos 23 Then \"Buy milk\" should not appear in the todo list 24 And the todo list should be empty 25"},{"url":"examples.html#the-internet","page":"Examples","section":"the-internet.feature","text":"Classic widgets: checkboxes, dropdowns, and a start URL per scenario. Source 1 Feature: The Internet (classic widgets) 2 3 @url:https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/checkboxes 4 Scenario: Toggle checkboxes 5 When I check checkbox 1 6 And I uncheck checkbox 2 7 Then checkbox 1 should be checked 8 And checkbox 2 should be unchecked 9 10 @url:https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/dropdown 11 Scenario: Pick from a dropdown 12 When I select \"Option 2\" in the dropdown 13 Then the dropdown should be \"Option 2\" 14 15 @url:https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/dynamic_loading/2 16 Scenario: Content that loads after a delay 17 When I load the example until the greeting is shown 18 Then I should see \"Hello World!\" 19 20 @url:https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/login 21 Scenario: Wrong password is rejected, right one logs in 22 When I try to log in as \"tomsmith\" with password \"wrong\" 23 Then the message should say \"Your password is invalid!\" 24 When I log in as \"tomsmith\" with password \"SuperSecretPassword!\" 25 Then the message should say \"You logged into a secure area!\" 26 27 @url:https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/tables 28 Scenario: Sorting a table by a column 29 When I sort the first table by last name 30 Then the first row of the first table should show \"Bach\" 31 32 @url:https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/javascript_alerts 33 Scenario: A confirm dialog reports the choice 34 When I open the JS confirm and cancel it 35 Then the result should say \"You clicked: Cancel\" 36"},{"url":"examples.html#github","page":"Examples","section":"github.feature","text":"A large live site with no login: tabs, headings and releases. Source 1 @url:https://github.com/microsoft/playwright 2 Feature: GitHub, a real site (public pages, no login) 3 Live site: cassettes replay while the recorded controls still match; changed ones heal with `--record new`. 4 5 Scenario: Find the latest release of a repository 6 When I open the releases page 7 Then the page heading should be \"Releases\" 8 And a release marked \"Latest\" should be shown 9 10 Scenario: Browse issues and filter by a label 11 When I open the Issues tab 12 Then the \"Issues\" tab should be selected 13 When I search the issues for \"label:bug\" 14 Then the issue list should show only issues labelled \"bug\" 15 16 Scenario: Read a file from the repository 17 When I open the \"package.json\" file 18 Then the file content should contain \"playwright-internal\" 19 And the \"Raw\" button should be shown 20 21 @url:https://github.com/ 22 Scenario: Search for a repository and open it 23 When I search GitHub for \"microsoft/playwright\" 24 And I open the \"microsoft/playwright\" repository from the results 25 Then the repository name \"playwright\" should be shown 26"}];
